                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "44abc252-2c92-30db-8e38-18fbf80c7183",
                        "entry_id": "bd9dccd3-4f9e-38c5-8bed-01ebe3987c31",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to convince, to persuade or to curb (to restrain/control), to make calm"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea6871e4-3e4e-4333-add4-7ba3dfa63810",
                                "sense_id": "44abc252-2c92-30db-8e38-18fbf80c7183",
                                "text": "Пья́ных мужико́в ча́стию урезо́нил, а ча́стию поучи́л руко́ю вла́стною, но с прия́тностью, так хорошо́, как бу́дто им э́тим большо́е одолже́ние сде́лал, и ничего́ не взял за нау́ку.",
                                "translation": "Some drunken muzhiks he brought to reason, and some he taught with his powerful hand, but with pleasantness, as nicely as if he were doing them a great favor, and he took nothing for the lesson.",
                                "english": "Some drunken muzhiks he brought to reason, and some he taught with his powerful hand, but with pleasantness, as nicely as if he were doing them a great favor, and he took nothing for the lesson."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
